Z||000000||rogergarrison||07-25-2001||09:54 PM||||Ive always wondered something. Has anyone ever bought a tape of the TV show that you just watched. You know like Discovery, A&E, History channel or Speedvision that they sell after the show for $19-$29? I may be missing something but if you want the tape that would mean you have a VCR right? My question is why would you buy something that you could tape yourself and put at least 6 shows on one tape to start with. If you would buy them, your out $20 per show and you have a mountain of tapes. And I think Im competent enough to make my own labels to find the program again. (scratching my head)||||reg||1
Z||000001||BC-GT||07-25-2001||10:02 PM||||School programs, teachers, institutions and the like I would presume. I have a cable modem, a CD burner and access to usenet, Why would I buy any software or music CD'S when I can "tape" it and put a label on it!?<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
